		""";
                          rdfs:domain swc:Call;
                          rdfs:label "has submission deadline";
                          rdfs:range xsd:dateTime;
                          status:term_status "deprecated".
swc:hasSubmissionInstructions a owl:DeprecatedProperty;
                              rdfs:comment """
			<p>The call classes have been deprecated in SWC. Instead, we suggest to use the <a href=\"http://sw.deri.org/2005/08/conf/cfp\">CfP ontology</a>.</p>
			
		""";
                              rdfs:domain swc:Call;
                              rdfs:label "has submission instructions";
                              rdfs:range xsd:string;
                              status:term_status "deprecated".
swc:hasTopic a owl:DeprecatedProperty;
             rdfs:comment """
			<p>Instead of this property, use <a href=\"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/topic\">foaf:topic</a>.</p>
			
		""";
             rdfs:label "has topic";
             rdfs:range swrc:ResearchTopic;
             status:term_status "deprecated".
swc:heldBy a owl:ObjectProperty;
           rdfs:comment """
			<p>
				Part of the <a href=\"#Role\">role</a> modelling machinery of SWC. This property relates a role at an event (e.g. a conference chair) to the person who actually holds the role.
			</p>
			
		""";
           rdfs:domain swc:Role;
           rdfs:label "held by";
           rdfs:range foaf:Person;
           owl:inverseOf swc:holdsRole;
           status:term_status "testing".
swc:holdsRole a owl:ObjectProperty;
              rdfs:comment """
			<p>
				Part of the <a href=\"#Role\">role</a> modelling machinery of SWC. This property relates a person to the role (e.g. a conference chair) it holds at an event.
			</p>
			
		""";
              rdfs:domain foaf:Person;
              rdfs:label "holds role";
              rdfs:range swc:Role;
              owl:inverseOf swc:heldBy;
              status:term_status "testing".
swc:isLocationFor a owl:ObjectProperty;
                  rdfs:comment """
			<p>
				Relates a location to a conference or sub-event thereof which takes place at it.
			</p>
			
		""";
                  rdfs:domain wgspos:SpatialThing;
                  rdfs:label "is location of";
                  rdfs:range swc:OrganisedEvent;
                  status:term_status "testing".
swc:isPartOf a owl:ObjectProperty;
             rdfs:comment """
			<p>
				A generic property to model part-of relationships. In SWC this property is used to relate papers or articles to the <a href=\"#Proceedings\">proceedings document</a> in which they are contained.
			</p>
			
		""";
             rdfs:domain owl:Thing;
             rdfs:label "is part of";
             rdfs:range owl:Thing;
             status:term_status "testing".
swc:isProvidedBy a owl:DeprecatedProperty;
                 rdfs:comment """
			<p>Deprecated because it has never been used and in order to reduce the inflation of ontology terms.</p>
			
		""";
                 rdfs:domain swc:Sponsorship;
                 rdfs:label "is provided by";
                 rdfs:range foaf:Organisation;
                 owl:inverseOf swc:isProviderOf;
                 status:term_status "deprecated".
swc:isProviderOf a owl:DeprecatedProperty;
                 rdfs:comment """
			<p>Deprecated because it has never been used and in order to reduce the inflation of ontology terms.</p>
			
		""";
                 rdfs:domain foaf:Organisation;
                 rdfs:label "is provider of";
                 rdfs:range swc:Sponsorship;
                 owl:inverseOf swc:isProvidedBy;
                 status:term_status "deprecated".
swc:isRoleAt a owl:ObjectProperty;
             rdfs:comment """
			<p>
				Part of the <a href=\"#Role\">role</a> modelling machinery of SWC. This property relates a role at an event (e.g. a conference chair) to the event (e.g. a conference).
			</p>
			
		""";
             rdfs:domain swc:Role;
             rdfs:label "is role at";
             rdfs:range swc:AcademicEvent;
             owl:inverseOf swc:hasRole;
             status:term_status "testing".
swc:isSubEventOf a owl:TransitiveProperty;
                 rdfs:comment "Events can be sub-events of other events. E.g., a talk can be a sub-event of a session, which in turn can be a sub-event of a conference. The relation is transitive - the talk is also a sub-event of the conference.";
                 rdfs:domain ical:Vevent;
                 rdfs:label "is sub-event of",
                            "is a sub-event of";
                 rdfs:range ical:Vevent;
                 owl:inverseOf swc:isSuperEventOf;
                 status:term_status "testing".
swc:isSuperEventOf a owl:TransitiveProperty;
                   rdfs:comment "Events can be super-events of other events. E.g., a conference can be the super-event of a session, which in turn can be the super-event of a talk. The relation is transitive - the conference is also the super-event of the talk.";
                   rdfs:domain ical:Vevent;
                   rdfs:label "is super-event of",
                              "is the super-event of";
                   rdfs:range ical:Vevent;
                   owl:inverseOf swc:isSubEventOf;
                   status:term_status "testing".
swc:isTopicOf a owl:DeprecatedProperty;
              rdfs:comment """
			<p>Deprecated, instead using terms from FOAF.</p>
			
		""";
              rdfs:domain swrc:ResearchTopic;
              rdfs:label "is topic of";
              status:term_status "deprecated".
swc:license_doc rdfs:comment """
			<!-- Creative Commons License -->
			<p class=\"copyright\">
				Copyright &copy; 2007-2009 Knud Möller, Sean Bechhofer and Tom Heath.<br/>
				<br/>
				<a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/\"><img alt=\"Creative Commons License\" style=\"border: 0; float: right; padding: 10px;\" src=\"somerights.gif\" /></a>
				This work is licensed under a <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/\">Creative Commons Attribution License</a>. 
				This copyright applies to the <em>Semantic Web Conference Ontology (SWC) Specification</em> and accompanying documentation in RDF.
				Regarding underlying technology, SWC uses W3C's <a href=\"http://www.w3.org/RDF/\">RDF</a> technology, an
				open Web standard that can be freely used by anyone.
			</p>
			
		""";
                rdfs:label "License Statement".
swc:memberOf a owl:ObjectProperty;
             rdfs:comment """
			<p>FOAF does not define an inverse of <code>foaf:member</code>, so SWC does it.</p>
			
		""";
             rdfs:domain foaf:Person;
             rdfs:label "member of";
             rdfs:range foaf:Group;
             owl:inverseOf foaf:member;
             status:term_status "testing".
swc:plansToAttend a owl:ObjectProperty;
                  rdfs:comment """
			<p>
				A person might plan to attend a talk or session at a conference or similar event. This property could be used to prepare a delegate's conference experience with respect to who they want to meet, etc.
			</p>
			
		""";
                  rdfs:domain foaf:Person;
                  rdfs:label "plans to attend";
                  rdfs:range swc:OrganisedEvent;
                  status:term_status "testing".
swc:relatedToEvent a owl:ObjectProperty;
                   rdfs:comment """
			<p>
				Relates a <a href=\"#ArgumentativeDocument\">document</a> to an <a href=\"#AcademicEvent\">event</a> such as a conference, workshop, etc.
			</p>
			
		""";
                   rdfs:domain swc:Artefact,
                               swc:ArgumentativeDocument;
                   rdfs:label "related to event",
                              "related to Event";
                   rdfs:range swc:AcademicEvent;
                   owl:inverseOf swc:hasRelatedDocument;
                   status:term_status "testing".
swc:uuid a owl:DeprecatedProperty;
         rdfs:label "uuid";
         status:term_status "deprecated".
